ULL,NULL,'Engineer here. I agree with you. Fahrenheit is for normal human experience. Celsius and Kelvin for scientific stuff.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2224,238,'instagram',NULL,'byond_limits',NULL,NULL,'80°F = 80% hot. 30°F =30% hot. Perfect system.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2225,238,'instagram',NULL,'kyleryanmcguire',NULL,NULL,'Fahrenheit allows for more precision within the window of most climates humans live in. The difference between 25 & 30 C is like 77 & 86 F. For weather, Fahrenheit is superior.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2226,238,'instagram',NULL,'carterpritchard03',NULL,NULL,'This is what we’ve been saying. Celsius is great for experiments, and engineers. But for people a scale of 0-100 is great. 0 is is cold af, 100 is hot af, 50 is a sweater, 75 is shorts and a t shirt. 90 means you can jump in a pool.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2227,238,'instagram',NULL,'alexcalamiatv',NULL,NULL,'American meteorologist here. Celsius wins 🙌0C is freezing 10C (50F) is cool20C (68F) is perfect 30C (86F) is hot 40C (104F) is brutal',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2228,238,'instagram',NULL,'alexcalamiatv',NULL,NULL,'alexcalamiatvVerified',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2229,238,'instagram',NULL,'sailing_songbird',NULL,NULL,'Been saying this for YEARS. Fahrenheit for weather. Celsius for cooking. Kelvin for nerds 💙',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2230,238,'instagram',NULL,'lafond_66',NULL,NULL,'Fahrenheit is useful because you can go by the 10s digit and have a very quick idea of the weather. For example - 30s is freezing, 50s is “chilly” - 70s is perfect, 90s is hot and 100+ is say indoors! You don’t need to know the exact temperature to know how to dress. Meanwhile, Celsius, 14 and 20 and HUGELY different.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2231,238,'instagram',NULL,'taylordrifts',NULL,NULL,'I hate the imperial system for many things. But temp and mph just feel right. Temp. 100. Hotttt. 70. Nice. 40. Cold. Like a percentage of hot. Then mph. 70. Quick. 100. Fast. Over 100. Real fast.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2232,238,'instagram',NULL,'taylordrifts',NULL,NULL,'taylordriftsVerified',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2233,238,'instagram',NULL,'the_maltesebeetroot',NULL,NULL,'NGL this is the best argument against Celcius I\'ve ever heard. And I\'m European.',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2234,238,'instagram',NULL,'northeast_alpine_start',NULL,NULL,'Avalanche educator here. My professional opinion: Celsius for snow, Fahrenheit for people. Meters for snowpack depth, feet for elevation, and everyone gets confused eventually. 😂',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2235,238,'instagram',NULL,'bored.bard',NULL,NULL,'Celsius for science, fahrenheit for weather (I understand weather is technically science)',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2236,238,'instagram',NULL,'bored.bard',NULL,NULL,'3w · Edited',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2237,238,'instagram',NULL,'kellyrizzo',NULL,NULL,'Fahrenheit is more precise. I need precision',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2238,238,'instagram',NULL,'kellyrizzo',NULL,NULL,'kellyrizzoVerified',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2239,238,'instagram',NULL,'victorvacheroncomedy',NULL,NULL,'More posts from victorvacheroncomedy',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2240,238,'instagram',NULL,'popular',NULL,NULL,'Popular',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 14:54:46'),(2241,239,'instagram',NULL,'mal.ntl.lab',NULL,NULL,'Also from Meta',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 09:55:02'),(2242,239,'instagram',NULL,'shoplibertythreads',NULL,NULL,'I LOVE THE USA BUTTON! 🇺🇸 ——>',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 09:55:02'),(2243,239,'instagram',NULL,'__amrit__0807',NULL,NULL,'Charger',NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-07 09:55:02'),(2244,239,'instagram',NULL,'shahrukh25',NULL,NULL,