 Re-entry Vehicle)\n\nThis advanced capability allows a single missile to carry multiple warheads and strike different targets simultaneously across a wide area. During the reported trial, multiple payloads were allegedly deployed toward separate targets in the Indian Ocean region, with tracking systems confirming successful mission performance.\n\nDefense analysts say the development significantly strengthens:\n🛡️ India’s strategic deterrence\n🎯 Long-range precision strike capability\n🚀 Indigenous defense technology advancement\n\nThe successful test also places India among a limited group of nations possessing advanced MIRV missile capability — a technology considered highly sophisticated in modern defense systems.\n\nAs news of the test spread online:\n🇮🇳 Many users praised India’s growing defense strength\n🔥 “Make in India” and self-reliance discussions trended\n⚔️ Strategic and geopolitical debates intensified online\n\nThe Agni missile program has long been considered one of India’s key pillars of national defense and strategic preparedness.\n\n💬 Advanced technology, precision capability, and deterrence remain central to modern national security. 🇮🇳\n\n#India #AgniV #MIRV #IndianDefence #MissileTest',1,'2026-05-11 05:00:00',15197,28,NULL,NULL,'positive',0.9,'[\"Bharat\"]','[]','[\"India\", \"Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Island\", \"Indian Ocean region\"]','[\"missile defense\", \"naval\", \"nuclear\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',98,'The post provides detailed information on India\'s successful test of an advanced Agni missile with MIRV capability, highlighting its strategic significance and implications for the country\'s defense capabilities.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 07:33:40','2026-07-07 07:34:54','2026-07-09 09:41:37'),(64,'facebook',NULL,NULL,'image',NULL,'Department of International Relations-NDU Pakistan',NULL,NULL,'The Department of International Relations is pleased to announce the appointment of Dr. Sumeera Imran as the new Head of the Department of