ming that global powers like China, Russia, and India are laughing at Europe’s \"eco-madness.\" 🌍📉\n\n​Tarczyński argues that while Europe contributes only 7% of global pollution, it is burdening its citizens with heavy costs while China, responsible for 30%, continues its growth. His message? It’s time for \"common sense\" to prevail. ✊⚖️\n\n​#Poland #Europe #EU #Geopolitics #CommonSense',1,'2026-05-02 05:00:00',95269,2827,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[\"Dominik Tarczyński\"]','[\"European Parliament\", \"EU\"]','[\"Poland\", \"Europe\"]','[\"Geopolitics\", \"CommonSense\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post discusses EU policies and global powers, but lacks specific details on military or missile defense aspects','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 12:53:24','2026-07-07 07:56:35','2026-07-09 09:42:07'),(112,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DXwhlGbyzUR/','DXwhlGbyzUR','video',NULL,'The Nations Radar',NULL,NULL,'Game changer for India 🔥🇮🇳\nContext: \nIndia’s Great Nicobar mega project, now officially estimated at around ₹81,000 crore, aims to build a transshipment port, airport, and township near key global shipping lanes. This strategic location can rival chokepoints like Hormuz, boosting India’s trade and military reach in the Indo-Pacific. However, its importance also makes it a potential target for both external adversaries seeking to limit India’s influence and internal disruptors opposing development. Securing this project is crucial, as it represents a long-term strategic asset for national security and economic dominance.\n\nLike👍, Share & Follow @thenationsradar for daily geopolitics📰🔥🌍 \n\nAndaman and Nicobar \nGreat Nicobar Mega Project \nStrait of Malacca \nIndia \nThe Nations Radar\n\n#geopolitics #indianpolitics #greatnicobar #andamanandnicobar #india',7,'2026-04-30 05:00:00',37113,1007,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[]','[\"India\"]','[\"Andaman and Nicobar\", \"Great Nicobar\", \"Strait of Malacca\", \"Hormuz\"]','[\"geopolitics\", \"indianpolit