trikes on Lebanon killing over 180 people and injuring hundreds in one of the deadliest days there with Beirut and other areas hit. Iran claims the truce was violated and has restricted shipping in the Strait of Hormuz while the US says the deal does not cover Lebanon. Vice President JD Vance will lead talks with Iran in Islamabad this weekend as President Trump warns of renewed action if terms are not met. Lebanon declared a day of mourning.\n\n.\n.\n.\n#edit #meme #politics #geopolitics #currentaffairs',1,'2026-04-09 05:00:00',502108,1802,NULL,NULL,'very_negative',-0.8,'[\"JD Vance\", \"President Trump\"]','[\"US\", \"Iran\", \"Israel\", \"Lebanon\"]','[\"Hormuz Strait\", \"Islamabad\", \"Beirut\", \"Lebanon\"]','[\"ceasefire\", \"airstrikes\", \"diplomacy\", \"geopolitics\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',71,'The post discusses a significant geopolitical event involving the US, Iran, and Israel, which are all relevant to strategic keywords','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 12:54:35','2026-07-07 07:56:35','2026-07-09 09:42:10'),(116,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DXMMGqBj104/','DXMMGqBj104','video',NULL,'GeoPoliticalXOfficial',NULL,NULL,'The partnership between Italian PM Giorgia Meloni and Indian PM Narendra Modi has significantly strengthened India-Italy relations, culminating in a \"Strategic Partnership\" elevated in 2023. Their close rapport, dubbed \"Melodi,\" has accelerated cooperation in defence, energy, technology, and economic ties, moving beyond past diplomatic tensions to a Joint Strategic Action Plan 2025-29. \n\nKey Aspects of the Meloni-Modi Era Relations:\n\nStrategic Partnership & The \"Melodi\" Brand: The relationship is characterized by high personal chemistry, famously highlighted by Meloni’s \"Melodi\" selfie at the 2024 G7 summit.\n\nDefense & Technology: Italy and India agreed to co-develop and co-produce defense equipment, diversifying India\'s security partners.\n\nEconomic and Trade Growth: Total trade between the two nations reached 13.76 US$ billion in 2024-25, with cooperation deepening in AI, space, and sustainable energy.\n\nJoint Strategic Action Plan (2025-29): The leaders have established a plan to deepen cooperation across 10 areas, including political dialogue, mobility, and cultural exchanges.\n\nGlobal Initiatives: Italy has joined several India-led initiatives, including the International Solar Alliance (ISA), Coalition for Disaster Resilient Infrastructure (CDRI), and the India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor (IMEEC).\n\nDefense Cooperation: A major shift from previous years saw a focus on defense co-production rather than just imports, following the resolution of the 2012 marines controversy. \n\nThe two leaders have reaffirmed their commitment to fostering a \"secure, modern, and progressive\" partnership, aligning with Italy\'s focus on the Indo-Pacific and India\'s role in the Mediterranean. \n\nThe partnership between Italian PM Giorgia Meloni and Indian PM Narendra Modi has significantly strengthened India-Italy relations, culminating in a \"Strategic Partnership\" elevated in 2023. Their close rapport, dubbed \"#Melodi,\" has accelerated cooperation in defence, energy, technology, and economic ties, moving beyond past diplomatic tensions to a Joint Strategic Action Plan 2025-29. #geopolitics #italy #modi #india',1,'2026-04-16 05:00:00',485092,3521,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[\"Giorgia Meloni\", \"Narendra Modi\"]','[\"Italian PM\", \"Indian PM\", \"G7 summit\"]','[\"Italy\", \"India\"]','[\"diplomacy\", \"trade\", \"defense cooperation\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post discusses the strengthening of India-Italy relations and cooperation in defense, energy, technology, and economic ties, but lacks specific details on military or missile defense aspects.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 07:54:50','2026-07-07 07:56:35','2026-07-09 09:42:11'),(117,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DYHjxS8IIe5/','DYHjxS8IIe5','video',NULL,'GEOCRUX',NULL,NULL,'Top 7 powerful countries in 2026 🌍🔥 \nBased on military, economy & global influence 👀\n___\n___\nTop 7 Powerful Countries (2026 – Overall Power)\n1️⃣ United States 🇺🇸\n👉 Military dominance + global influence + tech leadership\n2️⃣ China 🇨🇳\n👉 Massive economy + manufacturing + growing military\n3️⃣ Russia 🇷🇺\n👉 Nuclear arsenal + strategic military power\n4️⃣ India 🇮🇳\n👉 Fast-growing economy + rising global influence\n5️⃣ United Kingdom 🇬🇧\n👉 Strong alliances + finance + diplomacy\n6️⃣ France 🇫🇷\n👉 Nuclear power + global military presence\n7️⃣ Japan 🇯🇵\n👉 Technology + economic strength\n____\n___\nTAGS 🔑 \n#superpower #worldpower #geopolitics #usa #china \n_____\n_\nFollow for more @geocrux',1,'2026-05-09 05:00:00',107165,1935,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[]','[\"United States\", \"China\", \"Russia\", \"India\", \"United Kingdom\", \"France\", \"Japan\"]','[\"Global\", \"Asia\", \"Europe\", \"North America\", \"South Asia\"]','[\"geopolitics\", \"global influence\", \"military power\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post discusses global power rankings and military influence, but lacks specific details on missile defense or naval capabilities','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 07:55:22','2026-07-07 07:56:35','2026-07-09 09:42:12'),(118,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DZ7qc02KyB2/','DZ7qc02KyB2','video',NULL,'Julian dorey’s | Fan account',NULL,NULL,'Former CIA officer John Kiriakou shares a shocking look at how historic Christian communities in Palestine are rapidly disappearing.\n\nHe explains that the Christian population in the region has dropped from 10% down to just 2% or 3%. \n\nKiriakou argues that specific political and religious movements in the West have actually contributed to the destruction of these ancient communities. \n\nHis words challenge standard political talking points, forcing a completely new look at a highly complex global conflict.\n\nWatch the full breakdown to see why this perspective is sparking massive debate across social platforms.\n\n #geopolitics #historyfacts #podcastclips #worldnews #viralreels',1,'2026-06-23 05:00:00',39821,538,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-1,'[]','[\"CIA\"]','[\"Palestine\"]','[\"Christianity\", \"geopolitics\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post does not mention any of the strategic keywords (military, missile defense, naval, nuclear) and instead discusses Christian communities in Palestine, making it unrelated to the analysis lens.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 12:55:40','2026-07-07 07:56:35','2026-07-09 09:42:13'),(119,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DaViGz9h6pD/','DaViGz9h6pD','video',NULL,'Indian Diplomacy',NULL,NULL,'🇮🇳 India sent more than a delegation to Iran—it sent a strong message of unity: Many faiths, one nation.\n\nIndia sent an official delegation to Tehran to attend the funeral ceremonies of Iran\'s late Supreme Leader Ayatollah Seyyed Ali Khamenei. Led by senior Indian representatives, the delegation paid tributes on behalf of the Government of India and conveyed condolences to the Iranian leadership.\n\nThe visit came as world leaders and official delegations gathered in Tehran to honor the late leader. India\'s participation reflected the importance New Delhi attaches to its longstanding relationship with Iran and its commitment to maintaining diplomatic engagement during significant international events.\n\nFollow @indiandiplomecy for more‼️\n\n#India #Iran #IndianDiplomacy #Geopolitics',2,'2026-07-03 05:00:00',98443,1319,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[\"Ayatollah Seyyed Ali Khamenei\"]','[\"Government of India\", \"Iranian leadership\"]','[\"Tehran\", \"India\", \"Iran\"]','[\"diplomacy\", \"funeral ceremonies\", \"international relations\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post mentions India\'s diplomatic engagement with Iran, but does not provide specific details on military or missile defense aspects.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 12:56:14','2026-07-07 07:56:35','2026-07-09 09:42:14'),(120,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DYQQonRtD7n/','DYQQonRtD7n','video',NULL,'Nailyam Lutpulla',NULL,NULL,'Take a risk ✨ \n\n#womeninleadership #youthengagement #internationalrelations #studygram #unitednations',1,'2026-05-12 05:00:00',3,49,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-1,'[]','[]','[]','[\"leadership\", \"youth engagement\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post does not mention any of the strategic keywords (military, missile defense, naval, nuclear) and appears to be unrelated to international relations or global security issues.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 07:56:44','2026-07-07 07:59:43','2026-07-09 09:42:14'),(121,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DNnwKFJMuZ-/','DNnwKFJMuZ-','video',NULL,'Giulia Tariello',NULL,NULL,'How it feels to be underestimated in diplomacy… and how it feels to prove them wrong! \n\nIt is not a secret that, for too long, international spaces have not reflected the diversity of the world they represent. But now the trend is reversing. \n\nIt’s the reality that when someone discredit us and thinks we are not “enough”… we just prove them to be absolutely wrong. \n\nEvery time a young woman takes the mic, negotiates, shapes a policy and takes decisions, we rewrite the narrative. \n\n📌The G20 countries have increased women representation in diplomacy from 16,7% in 2018 to 21% in 2024 \n\n📌 Representation of women on the UN Security Council increased from 8% between 1990 and 2022 to 23% between 2015 -2024 \n \nWe are not just taking the space, we are changing it 🌏🌍🌎\n•\n•\n•\n#womenindiplomacy #diplomacy #internationalrelations #un #unitednations #unyouthdelegte #youth #motivation #inspo',9,'2025-08-21 05:00:00',14160,150,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[\"Giulia Tariello\"]','[]','[]','[\"women in diplomacy\", \"international relations\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post discusses the increasing representation of women in diplomacy and international relations, which is loosely related to the strategic keywords but lacks direct substance','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 07:57:42','2026-07-07 07:59:43','2026-07-09 09:42:15'),(122,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DZsavMSARw1/','DZsavMSARw1','video',NULL,'hina.osmuk',NULL,NULL,'Министр иностранных дел Турции Хакан Фидан о том, как эмоции и темперамент лидера влияют на принятие политических решений\n\n#мгимо \n#internationalrelations \n#turkey',10,'2026-06-17 05:00:00',2970,129,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.5,'[\"Hakan Yavas\"]','[]','[\"Turkey\"]','[\"politics\", \"international relations\"]','ru','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post discusses the personal characteristics of a Turkish minister, which is unrelated to military, missile defense, naval, or nuclear topics.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 07:58:27','2026-07-07 07:59:43','2026-07-09 09:42:15'),(123,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DaZ4AefyUNX/','DaZ4AefyUNX','video',NULL,'India Offscript',NULL,NULL,'🚨 A video from the Aligarh–Bulandshahr stretch of National Highway 34 has gone viral, showing a man allegedly stopping his vehicle to paste a large “Jaat” sticker onto an official government directional signboard while the act was being filmed.\n\nThe clip, reportedly recorded with the intention of being shared on social media, has sparked criticism online, with many questioning the defacement of public property and the use of community identity for viral content.\n\nGovernment signboards are public assets intended to provide important information for commuters. Damaging or altering them can create safety concerns and may violate the law.\n\nThe incident has also reignited conversations about responsible social media behavior, respect for public infrastructure, and the growing trend of performing risky or unlawful acts for online attention.\n\nDisclaimer:\nThis content is shared for informational, educational, and commentary purposes only. The information is based on publicly circulating videos and reports. The full circumstances and any legal action, if applicable, should be independently verified.\n\nCopyright Disclaimer:\nAny third-party visuals, footage, or materials belong to their respective owners and are used under fair use principles for commentary, criticism, education, and news reporting.\n\nAligarh, Bulandshahr, NH 34, Mahindra Thar, public property, highway signboard, viral video, social media, Uttar Pradesh, current affairs\n\n#PublicProperty #ViralVideo #CurrentAffairs',1,'2026-07-05 05:00:00',10553,247,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-1,'[]','[]','[\"Aligarh\", \"Bulandshahr\"]','[\"public property\", \"viral video\", \"current affairs\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post does not mention any of the strategic keywords (military, missile defense, naval, nuclear) and instead focuses on a unrelated incident about defacement of public property.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 08:00:29','2026-07-07 08:02:50','2026-07-09 09:42:16'),(124,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DZKfFqxi6Jt/','DZKfFqxi6Jt','video',NULL,'Cult Indians | Shivam Pandey',NULL,NULL,'Caught in a web of lies! 💍💼\nYou thought you married an IAS officer, but you actually married a walking, talking plot hole.\nThink your partner has a busy job? This man’s career was so “classified,” it didn’t even exist. 🕵️‍♂️✨\nMeet “Agent” Sandeep Singh \nFrom gonda who convinced an entire family he was an IAS officer and a high-level operative. Apparently, his “official duties” involved a transfer of ₹6.5 Lakhs from his in-laws. I suppose that’s one way to balance the national budget, right?\nWhile the family is left dealing with the reality of his “imaginary” career, local authorities are busy playing a game of hide-and-seek across Uttar Pradesh. Spoiler alert: The only thing “official” about this gentleman was how quickly he exited the scene.\nA gentle reminder: If your partner’s “Top Secret” government position involves asking for a loan from your parents, you aren’t living a spy movie—you’re just being misled.\nHashtags:\n#GondaUpdate #LifeLessons #Storytime #CurrentAffairs #TruthBeTold',1,'2026-06-04 05:00:00',531392,4368,NULL,NULL,'negative',-0.5,'[\"Sandeep Singh\"]','[]','[\"Gonda\", \"Uttar Pradesh\"]','[\"scam\", \"fraud\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post mentions a fictional character with a \'classified\' career, but the context is unrelated to military, missile defense, naval, or nuclear topics','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 08:00:55','2026-07-07 08:02:50','2026-07-09 09:42:17'),(125,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DYmhSm3IIMZ/','DYmhSm3IIMZ','video',NULL,'Narr.',NULL,NULL,'Pakistani actress Mamya Shajaffar used Iffat Omar\'s \'Say It All\' podcast as her platform to speak about what she describes as her worst on-set experience in the industry, and she didn\'t hold back. Calling out actor Arsalan Khan by name, Mamya alleged a pattern of unwanted physical contact, body-shaming comments made to co-workers, and a disturbing moment where he allegedly shook his belt at her during a disagreement about writer Manto\'s feminist legacy. A director reportedly had to intervene to keep the set functional. Mamya, who identifies as someone deeply uncomfortable with physical contact outside close friendships, said she was forced to shout before the behaviour stopped. The actress, known for her role in Lali, screened at the 76th Berlin Film Festival, also opened up about battling lupus and the psychological weight of deeply embodying characters. She later clarified on Instagram that she was referring specifically to this individual, amid online confusion over another actor sharing the same name. The interview has since been taken down.\n\n#pakistan \n#trending\n#lollywood\n#media\n#currentaffairs',1,'2026-05-21 05:00:00',2666,356,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-1,'[\"Mamya Shajaffar\", \"Arsalan Khan\"]','[]','[\"Pakistan\"]','[\"entertainment\", \"media\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post is unrelated to military, missile defense, naval, or nuclear topics and only mentions the keyword \'Pakistan\' in a non-strategic context','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 13:01:40','2026-07-07 08:02:50','2026-07-09 09:42:18'),(126,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DaX6DP5CDck/','DaX6DP5CDck','video',NULL,'Nocturne Smile',NULL,NULL,'In 2025, New York City animal shelters took in over 16,000 animals.\n\nNearly 10,000 were strays. Six thousand five hundred were owner surrenders.\n\nThat last number is the one that doesn\'t get talked about enough. Owner surrenders are not people who stopped caring. They are, in a significant portion of cases, people who cared and ran out of options. Pet food up 20 percent since 2022. Vet costs outpacing inflation for a decade. A city with a 25 percent poverty rate and some Bronx neighbourhoods where over 40 percent of residents are on SNAP.\n\nThe math on keeping a pet in New York has been quietly getting worse for years.\n\nMamdani\'s FY2027 budget, signed June 30, put 1.5 million dollars toward changing that. Seven hundred and fifty thousand for city-funded pet food pantries. Seven hundred and fifty thousand for affordable spay and neuter services. The first time New York City has ever put dedicated public dollars behind the idea.\n\nAnimal welfare advocates had been pushing for 15.3 million to fully fund pantries, vet clinics in every borough, and a real animal welfare office. They got roughly ten cents on the dollar of the full ask.\n\nIt is a fraction of what the problem actually costs. It is also more than the city has ever done before on this specific question.\n\nThe ASPCA called it a meaningful first step. Flatbush Cats, which has been running low-cost spay/neuter services on a shoestring budget, called it a foundation to build from.\n\nSometimes a government deciding something is worth doing at all is the move that matters. The number can grow. The precedent is harder to undo.\n\n#NYC #Mamdani #AnimalWelfare #CurrentAffairs #PowerAndControl',1,'2026-07-04 05:00:00',16877,471,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-1,'[\"New York City residents\"]','[\"New York City animal shelters\", \"Flatbush Cats\", \"ASPCA\"]','[\"New York City\", \"Bronx\"]','[\"animal welfare\", \"poverty rate\", \"pet food prices\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post does not mention military, missile defense, naval, or nuclear topics at all.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 08:02:08','2026-07-07 08:02:50','2026-07-09 09:42:18'),(127,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/Dacw_wmCVsb/','Dacw_wmCVsb','video',NULL,'Narmin Karimova',NULL,NULL,'Mosque Controversy Sparks Debate in Japan\n\nA dispute has emerged in Japan over a mosque project that local authorities reportedly say did not receive the necessary approvals before construction.\n\nAccording to reports, the issue gained further attention after Pakistan\'s ambassador attended the inauguration ceremony. Local officials are now reviewing the matter, and questions are being raised about compliance with municipal regulations and building permits.\n\nThe controversy has also fueled a broader debate in Japan over immigration, cultural integration, and the impact of rapid demographic changes on local communities.\n\nSupporters argue that religious freedom should be protected, while critics insist that all construction projects must strictly follow local laws and regulations.\n\nAs the situation develops, it is becoming a focal point in discussions about governance, community relations, and cultural change in Japan.\n\nWhat do you think should authorities focus solely on legal compliance, or does this reflect a larger debate about immigration and integration?\n\n#japannews #pakistannews #tokyotokyo #geopolitics #worldnews #breakingnewsnow #internationalrelations #immigration #culturaldebate #currentaffairs #asianews #globalpolitics #newsupdate #trendingnews',1,'2026-07-06 05:00:00',63214,3433,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-1,'[]','[]','[\"Japan\"]','[\"immigration\", \"cultural integration\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',0,'The post does not mention any of the strategic keywords (military, missile defense, naval, nuclear) and instead focuses on a mosque controversy in Japan with no apparent connection to these topics.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 13:02:35','2026-07-07 08:02:50','2026-07-09 09:42:19'),(128,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DXCTcVjCmvE/','DXCTcVjCmvE','video',NULL,'NextShark',NULL,NULL,'Thai men across the country faced a high-stakes military conscription lottery this April, as tensions linger along Thailand’s disputed border with Cambodia following deadly clashes last year. At a temple near Bangkok, men aged 18 to 29 drew cards that determined their fate, with black granting exemption and red requiring enlistment.⁠\n⁠\nConscripts serve up to two years, while volunteers serve shorter terms and receive a monthly salary along with basic provisions. While some expressed relief at avoiding service, others accepted their outcome with composure, as families watched anxiously and reflected on duty, livelihood and honor.⁠\n⁠\n📽️Editor: Gabe Jung⁠\n🤳Click our linkinbio to sign up to our daily newsletter.⁠ ⁠⁠\n📰Follow us for the latest Asian News @NextShark⁠ ⁠ ⁠\n⁠\n#thailand #military #conscription #draftlottery #bangkok #cambodia #borderconflict #southeastasia #news #asiannews #breakingnews #militaryservice #nationalism #economy #jobs #youth #society #culture #temple #lottery #army #navy #airforce #geopolitics #worldnews #currentevents #recruitment #asia',1,'2026-04-12 05:00:00',548027,8330,NULL,NULL,'neutral',-0.2,'[\"Thai men\"]','[\"NextShark\"]','[\"Thailand\", \"Cambodia\"]','[\"military conscription\", \"draft lottery\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',46,'The post discusses military conscription in Thailand, which is loosely related to missile defense and naval capabilities, but lacks direct strategic substance.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 13:03:02','2026-07-07 08:05:41','2026-07-09 09:42:20'),(129,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DJ7B2QmvnOl/','DJ7B2QmvnOl','video',NULL,'Just 60 words',NULL,NULL,'Following the recent India-Pakistan conflict in the wake of Operation Sindoor, reports indicate a strong Chinese presence and influence on the Pakistani side. A new report suggests that Beijing provided Islamabad with satellite and air defense support to monitor Indian troop movements. Chinese involvement may have encouraged Pakistan to retaliate despite India’s non-escalatory measures. This has resulted in heightened tensions along the India-Pakistan border.\n\nTies between Islamabad and Beijing have steadily grown stronger. Pakistani Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Mohammad Ishaq Dar met with Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi in a high-level meeting on 20 May. Wang Yi reaffirmed China’s support for Pakistan, underscoring their deepening alliance.\n\n[India, Pakistan, Operation Sindoor, China, Satellite Support, Air Defense, Islamabad, Beijing, Mohammad Ishaq Dar, Wang Yi, Military Alliance, Border Conflict, Regional Tensions, Strategic Partnership, Diplomacy]\n\n#india #pakistan #china #operation #sindoor #borderconflict #indiapakistanrelations #chinasupport #satellitedefense #airdefense #militaryalliance #diplomacy #foreignrelations #southasia #regionaltensions #wangyi #mohammadishaqdar #defense #strategicpartnership #geopolitics #bordersecurity',1,'2025-05-21 05:00:00',241,17,NULL,NULL,'negative',-0.5,'[\"Mohammad Ishaq Dar\", \"Wang Yi\"]','[\"China\", \"Pakistan\", \"India\"]','[\"Asia\", \"South Asia\", \"Pakistan\", \"India\", \"Beijing\", \"Islamabad\"]','[\"Military Alliance\", \"Border Conflict\", \"Regional Tensions\", \"Diplomacy\", \"Geopolitics\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',71,'The post provides specific details on Chinese involvement in the India-Pakistan conflict and its potential impact on regional tensions','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-07 08:04:11','2026-07-07 08:05:41','2026-07-09 09:42:21'),(130,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DZg9BOKu7id/','DZg9BOKu7id','video',NULL,'STUDY IAS PCS',NULL,NULL,'\"क्या आपको पता है? भारत और नेपाल के बीच सुस्ता नदी विवाद सदियों से चला आ रहा है। जानिए, कैसे गंडक