ICBM with a projected range exceeding 10,000 km, significantly boosting India\'s strategic deterrence capabilities. While gamers worldwide are still counting down to GTA VI (now slated for November 2026), India\'s missile scientists might deliver Agni-VI much sooner once they get the green light.\nThis light-hearted meme perfectly captures the national pride: India\'s defence prowess could outpace even the most hyped entertainment releases. 🇮🇳\n#AgniVI #DRDO #AgniMissile #IndianDefence #AtmanirbharBharat',NULL,'2026-04-30 05:00:00',3,33,NULL,NULL,'positive',0.8,'[\"ARYA BHARATVANSHI\", \"Dr. Samir V Kamat\"]','[\"DRDO\", \"ANI\"]','[\"India\"]','[\"missile defense\", \"naval\", \"nuclear\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',71,'The post directly mentions the Agni-VI missile and its development status, providing strategic substance on India\'s military capabilities.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-08 09:52:14','2026-07-08 04:57:28','2026-07-09 09:44:18'),(310,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/C5TwdoSPl2t/','C5TwdoSPl2t','video',NULL,'Milan Nakum',NULL,NULL,'Agni Prime with MARV+MIRV capability successfuly tested tonight by DRDO.\n..\n#drdo \n#agni \n#agnimissile \n#test \n#marv',NULL,'2024-04-03 05:00:00',1962,6,NULL,NULL,'positive',0.8,'[\"Milan Nakum\"]','[\"DRDO\"]','[]','[\"missile defense\", \"naval\", \"nuclear\"]','en','llama3.2:latest',95,'The post directly mentions a successful test of Agni Prime with MARV+MIRV capability by DRDO, indicating a significant development in India\'s missile defense capabilities.','{\"source\": \"yt-dlp\"}','2026-07-08 04:52:42','2026-07-08 04:57:28','2026-07-09 09:44:18'),(311,'instagram','https://www.instagram.com/p/DXwa-rKh0_A/','DXwa-rKh0_A','video',NULL,'@globalmarkettracker',NULL,NULL,'Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO) Chairman Samir V Kamat said the much-anticipated Agni VI ballistic missile programme will move forward the moment the government gives its approval. Speaking at the ANI National Security Summit 2.0, he noted that the agency has completed all groundwork and is positioned to begin once the formal nod comes.\n\nAgni VI is expected to become the most advanced missile in India\'s Agni series, featuring a significantly greater reach and improved performance. While the project remains tied to a policy decision, DRDO\'s readiness suggests India is gearing up for another major upgrade in its strategic arsenal.\n\nKamat highlighted strong progress in India\'s hypersonic systems, particularly the LR AShM glide missile. According to him, initial trials for the glide variant are not far off. \"With respect to the hypersonic, we are working on two programs, the Hypersonic Glide Missile and the Hypersonic Cruise Missile,\" he added.\n\nKamat further explained how the glide system relies on a booster for initial acceleration before travelling without propulsion, while the cruise system depends on a scramjet engine throughout its flight.\n\nThe DRDO chief also spoke about the evolving structure of a proposed conventional missile force and stressed that it must include a broad mix of capabilities from short to long range. He said the force would need ballistic missiles across multiple ranges along with cruise and hypersonic systems\n\nfor tactical and strategic missions.\n\nKamat pointed out that short-range platforms are almost ready for induction. He said the Pralay system is in its final testing stages and could join the armed forces soon.\n\nThe Agni-VI is a proposed next-generation, nuclear-capable Intercontinental Ballistic Missile (ICBM) being developed by DRDO. It has been designed for a 12,000-16,000 km range. It is also expected to feature advanced MIRV technology.\n\nAgni VI aims to enhance India\'s nuclear deterrence posture with improved accuracy, survivability and payload flexibility.\n\n#drdo #agnimissile #defencetechnology #india \n #trendingreels',NULL,'2026-04-30 05:00:00',3912,22,NULL,NULL,'neutral',0.8,'[]','[\"DRDO\", \"India\"]','[\"India\"]','[